<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Reading path</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Kingdoms of Southeast Asia</h1><p class="ws-lede">Follow the trading ports, temple cities and sultanates of mainland and island Southeast Asia.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/paths/kingdoms-of-southeast-asia">Open the path &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the stops from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest), by when each began: a state&#8217;s founding, a person&#8217;s birth, the date of an event.</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Khmer Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Pagan Kingdom</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Funan</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Champa</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Srivijaya Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Chenla</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">The path uses these words. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Chao (currency)</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Entrepôt</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Reservoir</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Spice trade</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Stop 1, <b>Funan</b>. The path begins here because: &#8220;Generally considered the first known kingdom of Southeast Asia, Funan traded through its port of Óc Eo, where Roman gold medallions and Indian and Persian goods were found.&#8221; What does this stop tell you about how the story began?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 6, <b>Khmer Empire</b>: &#8220;Founded in 802, the empire ruled much of mainland Southeast Asia from Angkor, where vast reservoirs and canals paid for Angkor Wat and Angkor Thom.&#8221; Find one detail on its page that supports this, and one question it leaves open.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 10, <b>Malacca Sultanate</b>: &#8220;Founded about 1400 by Parameswara under Ming protection, the port became the great entrepôt of the strait and a centre of Islamic learning until the Portuguese took it in 1511.&#8221; How does this last stop connect to an earlier one?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The path sums itself up as: &#8220;Follow the trading ports, temple cities and sultanates of mainland and island Southeast Asia.&#8221; Which stop shows this best? Explain your choice.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/paths/kingdoms-of-southeast-asia. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Kingdoms of Southeast Asia</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Funan <span>from 50 CE</span></li><li>Champa <span>from 192 CE</span></li><li>Chenla <span>from 550 CE</span></li><li>Srivijaya Empire <span>from 650 CE</span></li><li>Khmer Empire <span>from 802 CE</span></li><li>Pagan Kingdom <span>from 849 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Chao (currency)</dt><dd>Chao was the paper currency issued by the Yuan Dynasty in China.</dd><dt>Entrepôt</dt><dd>An entrepôt is a port or trading centre where goods are imported, stored and re-exported, often without further processing.</dd><dt>Reservoir</dt><dd>A reservoir is an artificial or enlarged body of water used to store water for irrigation, drinking or flood control.</dd><dt>Spice trade</dt><dd>The spice trade was the long-distance commerce in spices such as pepper, cinnamon, cloves and nutmeg from South and Southeast Asia.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the pages of the path.</p></section></div></details>
